</div></div>
<div class="note"><p><strong>Why.</strong> Two reasons on this page spoke of the coordinator as “you”, as the skill does when it speaks to its own reader, and you read that “you” as yourself; your comments of 16:38 and 16:40. The first commit put the rule into the bullet on the form of a landed item, so it reached only a landed item's reason. The cold read found that the “why” of a proposed item, and any other text a worker writes on a page, could still say “you”. The second commit took the sentence out of that bullet and made it a bullet of its own, for every text on every page. So the bullet on the landed item reads as it did before.</p></div>
